{
  "out": "/tmp/photonz-playtest/the-speed-curve-shows-under-a-clip-walk",
  "seed": "At Next defaults, with no switch touched: the tutorial recording (eight seconds). Two speed stops go on from the clip's right click, at three and six seconds, and the clip's speed curve opens under it on the timeline with the mock's 3x, 1x and 0 scale, all Normal. The second stop is dragged straight up by a real pointer to 2.5x: the curve, the clip and the picture follow the hand, the Fast band inks the mock's #ff5d8f along the floor, and it is one step to undo. The third stop is then made a Freeze from its Speed list: two zeros side by side, the band between them hatched in amber, and the freeze's second zero drags the hold longer. Every band is read off the window's own picture where the lane drew it, and the dashed 1x line within a point of where the scale puts it.",
  "setup": {
    "timelineOpen": true,
    "front": true,
    "forget": [
      "all"
    ]
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "do": "action",
      "action": "openSampleRecording"
    },
    {
      "do": "wait",
      "seconds": 2.0
    },
    {
      "do": "action",
      "action": "videoPause"
    },
    {
      "do": "tool",
      "tool": "select"
    },
    {
      "do": "wait",
      "seconds": 0.6
    },
    {
      "do": "clickRuler",
      "seconds": 3.0
    },
    {
      "do": "wait",
      "seconds": 0.4
    },
    {
      "do": "rightClick",
      "on": "Tutorial Sample clip",
      "across": 0.375,
      "choose": "Speed > Add Speed Stop at 0:03.00"
    },
    {
      "do": "wait",
      "seconds": 0.6
    },
    {
      "do": "clickRuler",
      "seconds": 6.0
    },
    {
      "do": "wait",
      "seconds": 0.4
    },
    {
      "comment": "The first stop opened the curve under the clip and the timeline scrolled to show it.",
      "do": "reveal",
      "control": "Tutorial Sample clip"
    },
    {
      "do": "rightClick",
      "on": "Tutorial Sample clip",
      "across": 0.75,
      "choose": "Speed > Add Speed Stop at 0:06.00"
    },
    {
      "do": "wait",
      "seconds": 0.8
    },
    {
      "do": "expectClip",
      "clip": "Tutorial Sample",
      "startsAt": 0,
      "endsAt": 8,
      "within": 0.02
    },
    {
      "do": "wait",
      "seconds": 0.4
    },
    {
      "comment": "THE FIRST TEST: the clip's speed curve is open under it with four stops, all Normal, on the clip's own clock.",
      "do": "expectSpeedCurve",
      "clip": "Tutorial Sample",
      "bands": [
        "normal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "comment": "A Command-click on the line adds a stop there at the speed the line already has, the rule every animated line follows (a plain click picks). The check above scrolled the curve into sight, its plot at window (160, 874) and 1556pt across, so seven seconds in on the 1x line is (1521, 936).",
      "do": "windowClick",
      "at": [
        1521,
        936
